operty for nearly 40  years  he thinks his grandson's survival is  unbelievable  it's just amazing he survived  i don't even know if i would have lived  for that long  on sunday three-year-old jude layton  went missing here  police and volunteer crews combed woods  and water  day and night at times temperatures were  below freezing  it's a very treacherous area if you  wander off you know you can you can  it's quite easy to get lost even i've  been turned around on the property  myself from  sunday all the way to wednesday this  clearing that's empty now  was full with people with vehicles  fisher says two helicopters landed here  until the best moment on wednesday when  through that clearing  officers brought jude home on an atv  that's the best day i've had in the opp  in 25 years it was constable scott  mcnamee's birthday when he got the call  to help  he searched for three days it was rocky  it was steep  i'll be honest i did not think that a  three-year-old almost four-year-old  would be able to get that far back there  then less than a kilometer from the  family compound  mcnames spotted something blue another  officer ran  up ahead he said he's here he was lying  down on the stomach and then  jude the little boy raised his head and  opened his eyes and he said and he's  alive  mcnamee says jude was wet but warm  he thinks his wool sweater may have  saved him he asked for some water  he's a tough little guy for sure the  last year  has been just horrendous for everybody  and  this is something that should be  uplifting to  to everybody across the country jude is  in hospital with his parents still being  checked out  the family is so grateful for everyone's  support and for an unbelievably happy  outcome  at a time when everyone can use an extra  smile  abigail beeman global news south  frontinak ontario  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen tonight's  your canada  is this great grey owl in foothills  alberta  there are beautiful sp